@startuml
title COLORS - Class Diagram
top to bottom direction

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam dpi 140
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #F2F6FC
skinparam ClassBorderColor #333333
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam nodesep 80
skinparam ranksep 55
hide circle
hide empty members

class "js/code.js" as Browser <<module>> {
  userId : Integer
  firstName : String
  lastName : String
  --
  +doLogin() : void
  +doLogout() : void
  +addColor() : void
  +searchColor() : void
  +saveCookie() : void
  +readCookie() : void
}

together {
  class "Login.php" as Login <<endpoint>> {
    +POST(login, password)
  }
  class "AddColor.php" as Add <<endpoint>> {
    +POST(color, userId)
  }
  class "SearchColors.php" as Search <<endpoint>> {
    +POST(search, userId)
  }
}

class User <<entity>> {
  ID : Integer
  firstName : String
  lastName : String
  Login : String
  Password : String
}

class Color <<entity>> {
  Name : String
  UserID : Integer
}

Browser ..> Login : calls
Browser ..> Add : calls
Browser ..> Search : calls

Login ..> User : reads
Add ..> Color : inserts
Search ..> Color : searches

User "1" -right- "0..*" Color : owns

' Lecture references:
' Introduction to UML.pdf, slides 5-12 (names and attributes; operations are optional),
' 18-21 (association and multiplicity), and 42 (class-diagram example).
' PA-chapter06-Revised.ppt, section 6.4 (object types, attributes, static relationships).
'
' Scope: logical class view of the implemented modules and data entities.
' The module stereotype groups the existing JavaScript variables and functions.
' Endpoint POST operations describe HTTP request contracts, not PHP function names.
' User and Color correspond to records in the Users and Colors tables. The source
' is procedural; this diagram does not assert that these are implemented OO classes.
' Attributes use logical UML types and the names referenced by the application.
' Browser constants, the MD5 library internals, PHP JSON helper functions, and
' transient request/response data are omitted for clarity.
'
' Source verification:
' js/code.js defines userId, firstName, lastName, and all six shown functions.
' doLogin(), addColor(), and searchColor() call the corresponding PHP endpoints.
' doLogout() clears browser state and redirects; no logout endpoint is implemented.
' LAMPAPI/Login.php: SELECT ID,firstName,lastName FROM Users WHERE Login=? AND Password=?
' LAMPAPI/AddColor.php: INSERT into Colors (UserId,Name) VALUES(?,?)
' LAMPAPI/SearchColors.php: SELECT Name FROM Colors WHERE Name LIKE ? AND UserID=?
' SQL uses both UserId and UserID spellings; this model normalizes the attribute to UserID.
' js/code.js sends an MD5 hash as the login password and uses userId for add/search.
'
' A User may have no saved colors or many, and each Color in the normal application
' data is associated with one User ID. The plain association is labeled "owns" in
' the domain sense; this does not assert composition or cascade deletion.
' The repository contains no table-creation schema, so foreign-key enforcement,
' deletion rules, and additional fields such as Color.ID are not assumed.
' No Session.id or ColorService class is added because the implementation does not
' establish those structures. No getters, setters, or entity methods are invented.
@enduml
